# AGENTS.md: {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}. User-facing docs: `README.md`.

## Layout

{% if entrypoint == 'entrypoint' -%}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/`: the package; `{{ script_target }}` is the console
  script `{{ project_name }}`, the image's entry point.
{%- elif entrypoint == 'cmd' -%}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/`: the package; `{{ script_target }}` is the console
  script `{{ project_name }}`, the image's default command. A deployment's
  command picks another script from `[project.scripts]`.
{%- else -%}
- `src/{{ package_name }}/`: the package. The image has no entry point: each
  deployment's command names a console script from `[project.scripts]`.
{%- endif %}
- `tests/`: pytest. Keep I/O out of the logic so it tests without mocks.
- `Dockerfile`: two stages, `uv sync --locked` into `/opt/venv`, then a
  runtime without pip.

## Conventions

{% if ships_releases -%}
- Conventional Commits, header at most 72 characters. The commit subjects
  that reach main are the release notes: `feat`/`fix`/`perf` release, `refactor`,
  `test`, `docs`, `ci`, `chore` don't (a dependency update to runtime files
  ships in the weekly maintenance release). CI lints every commit with
  [commitlint-config-mbologna](https://github.com/mbologna/commitlint-config)
  and rejects `fixup!` commits; pull requests merge with a merge commit.
{%- elif changelog_releases -%}
- Conventional Commits, header at most 72 characters. The commit subjects
  that reach main are the changelog: `feat`/`fix`/`perf` release, `refactor`,
  `test`, `docs`, `ci`, `chore` don't (a dependency update to runtime files
  goes into the weekly maintenance release). CI lints every commit with
  [commitlint-config-mbologna](https://github.com/mbologna/commitlint-config)
  and rejects `fixup!` commits; pull requests merge with a merge commit.
- Every push to main that changes the image publishes it as `latest` and
  `sha-<commit>`{% if cloud_run != 'none' %} and deploys it, by digest, to the Cloud Run {{ cloud_run }}{% endif %}.
{%- else -%}
- Conventional Commits, header at most 72 characters. CI lints every commit
  with [commitlint-config-mbologna](https://github.com/mbologna/commitlint-config)
  and rejects `fixup!` commits; pull requests merge with a merge commit.
- Every push to main that changes the image publishes it as `latest` and
  `sha-<commit>`{% if cloud_run != 'none' %} and deploys it to the Cloud Run {{ cloud_run }}{% endif %}.
{%- endif %}
- Coverage may not drop below `fail_under` in `pyproject.toml`; raise it
  when tests are added.
- Dependencies: `uv add <pkg>`; uv.lock is committed and the image installs
  it with `--locked`. `exclude-newer` keeps releases younger than 7 days out.
{%- if notifications %}
- Notifications go through `apprise_notify.notify()` with the `APPRISE_URL`
  environment variable: one URL or several space-separated ones, tried in
  order. It never raises; check its return value when sending matters.
{%- endif %}
- The image: non-root (uid {{ image_uid }}), no pip, nothing written outside `/tmp`{% if writable_dirs.split() %},
  {% for d in writable_dirs.split() %}`{{ d }}`{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '' }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
  or a mounted volume.
- One program in the image is its `ENTRYPOINT`, and flags go in the
  container's arguments. With several programs the image has a default
  `CMD`, or none, and a deployment's command picks one.

## Versioning

{% if ships_releases -%}
Plain SemVer: `vX.Y.Z` tags, each building and pushing the image as
`X.Y.Z`, `X.Y` and `latest`, per the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).

- Never create, move or delete tags, and never edit a version number to cut
  a release: auto-release tags from the commit types (`feat` minor; `fix`,
  `perf`, `revert` patch; `!` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer major).
- Write Conventional Commit subjects; they decide the next version.
- `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and stays `0.0.0`; the
  image's `org.opencontainers.image.version` label comes from the tag.
{%- elif changelog_releases -%}
Plain SemVer, per the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md):
`vX.Y.Z` tags with a GitHub Release each, a changelog of what main already
{% if cloud_run != 'none' %}deployed{% else %}published{% endif %}. A tag builds no image.

- Never create, move or delete tags, and never edit a version number to cut
  a release: auto-release tags from the commit types (`feat` minor; `fix`,
  `perf`, `revert` patch; `!` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer major).
- Write Conventional Commit subjects; they decide the next version.
- `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and stays `0.0.0`.
{%- else -%}
Unversioned: no tags and no releases, per the
[versioning standard](https://github.com/mbologna/.github/blob/main/VERSIONING.md).

- Don't create tags or Releases; nothing would build from them.
- `version` in `pyproject.toml` is a placeholder and stays `0.0.0`.
{%- endif %}

## Template

The skeleton comes from https://github.com/mbologna/python-app-template
(`.copier-answers.yml`). Renovate's copier manager opens a pull request
for each template release; resolve conflicts in favour of this project's
code. By hand: `uvx copier update`, then `uv lock` if dependencies changed.
To change an answer: `uvx copier update -d <question>=<value>`.
